                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Neat and orderly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e760c5b-1a28-4977-a3d8-5d0642b10379",
                                                "sense_id": "765bd8d1-8f88-3c5f-b87f-d89df7a99cab",
                                                "text": "What is certain is that everything they see is strange: the lifeless neatness of the courtyard, the straightness of the paths, the ruly gang of labourers in their dull uniforms and with their ageless, polished faces."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9fb2461b-3122-45e4-931f-3130d6b75b54",
                                                "sense_id": "765bd8d1-8f88-3c5f-b87f-d89df7a99cab",
                                                "text": "1610: John Marston, Histrio-Mastix, page 28 (quarto): [Perpetuana:] Nay Ile be matchlesse for a carckanet,/Whose Pearles and Diamonds plac'd with ruly rocks/Shall circle this faire necke to set it forth [.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
